GPL-3.0 — see the full text at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.txt

Why GPL-3.0 for this repo: the reimplemented pipeline tools and scripts are
part of a voice-training workflow whose upstream components are GPLv3
(piper1-gpl teacher training, sanoTTS training/G2P side), and GPL keeps the
resulting contributions compatible with both projects.

License boundaries of everything this repo drives (unchanged from upstream):

- piper1-gpl (teacher training + export): GPLv3. Its outputs (the ONNX
  voice) are data; the piper-voices collection is distributed under each
  voice's dataset license.
- sanoTTS runtime: MIT. sanoTTS training/G2P side: GPLv3.
- The es_CL voice weights themselves: CC BY-SA 4.0 via the SLR71 dataset
  (see ATTRIBUTION.txt).
- Tatoeba training text: CC BY 2.0 FR.
